1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,500
Hey everyone! Today I am demonstrating a brand new autonomous skill built for Mermail: the Autonomous Invoice and Micro-Bounty Settler.

2
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:21,000
Traditional AI agents can draft emails and generate code, but until now, they could not autonomously settle financial obligations directly from an agent inbox without human intervention.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:33,500
With Mermail providing both an AI-first mailbox and a user-controlled Agent Wallet over the Model Context Protocol, autonomous agents can now monitor invoices, inspect deliverables, and settle on-chain bounties safely.

4
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:45,820
In this video, I will show the complete workflow: triggering the skill, connecting to Mermail, executing the on-chain transfer on Solana, and delivering a cryptographic email receipt.

5
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:55,500
Let us examine the SKILL.md file that defines this agent capability. The skill is titled mermail-invoice-settler.

6
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:05,500
It equips the agent with clear instructions, pre-flight safety policies, and structured tool definitions.

7
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Specifically, the agent connects to the Mermail MCP server, utilizing search_emails to monitor incoming bounty submissions, get_paybox_connection to authenticate the embedded Agent Wallet, and get_agent_wallet_portfolio to verify liquidity.

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:27,500
Notice our security policy: we enforce a strict 100 USDC per-transaction safety ceiling and mandatory deliverable verification before any on-chain transfer can be dispatched.

9
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:35,760
Once approved, paybox_request_transfer executes the payment, and reply_to_email delivers the final transaction proof.

10
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:45,500
Now let us watch the live demonstration in our agent terminal.

11
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:56,500
We trigger the skill with the prompt: 'Check my Mermail inbox for contractor invoice emails, verify the PR deliverables, check our wallet liquidity, and settle verified claims under 100 USDC with receipt.'

12
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:05,000
Watch as the agent initializes and connects to the Mermail Model Context Protocol server.

13
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Step 1: The agent polls the inbox and finds an unread invoice from contributor@solana-builder.org, requesting 35 USDC for completing Pull Request number 14.

14
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Step 2: The agent parses the contributor Solana address and deliverable link.

15
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Step 3: It queries the Mermail Agent Wallet, confirming an available balance of 250 USDC. The 35 USDC invoice is well within our 100 USDC safety policy.

16
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:43,500
Step 4: The agent invokes paybox_request_transfer to execute the on-chain USDC transfer on Solana.

17
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:52,370
And look at that: transaction confirmed! Signature 5Kj Solana Sig Alpha 99 is emitted, and the agent immediately dispatches an itemized email receipt with the Solscan explorer link.

18
00:02:52,370 --> 00:03:01,500
Finally, let us review the verified outcome. On the right panel, the Solana Explorer card confirms the on-chain transfer of 35 USDC has finalized.

19
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:12,500
Our Agent Wallet reflects the updated balance of 215 USDC, and the contractor has received an automated email receipt containing the cryptographic transaction signature.

20
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:19,500
The unread invoice has been cleanly marked as processed.

21
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:28,500
This proves how Mermail bridges communication and capital, enabling reliable, autonomous contractor payouts and DAO micro-grants.

22
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:36,409
The complete skill has been submitted as an open-source pull request to the official Mermail skills repository. Thank you for watching!

